EXHIBIT B
FULL TEXT BALLOT PROPOSITION
SAN BERNARDINO COMMUNITY COLLEGE DISTRICT
BOND MEASURE ELECTION NOVEMBER 3, 2026
“Local College Affordability, Job Training, Repairs Measure. To maintain affordable college
education access, by repairing /upgrading San Bernardino Valley College, Crafton Hills College;
preparing students/ veterans for high-demand careers including skilled trades, firefighting, healthcare;
providing safe drinking water; removing asbestos, mold; repairing deteriorating gas lines; acquiring,
constructing, repairing facilities, sites, equipment; shall San Bernardino Community College District’s
measure authorizing $898,000,000 in bonds at legal rates, levying $25 per $100,000 of assessed
valuation ($56,000,000 annually) while bonds are outstanding, requiring oversight, audits, be
adopted?”
Bonds - Yes Bonds – No
PROJECTS
The Board of Trustees of the San Bernardino Community College District, to be responsive to
the needs of its community, evaluated San Bernardino Valley College and Crafton Hills College’s
urgent and critical facility needs, and its capacity to provide students, and Veterans with support and
job training facilities, an affordable education and prepare them for success in college and careers
and skilled trades. Job training facilities, safety issues, class size and offerings, and information and
computer technology were each considered in developing the types of projects to be funded by this
measure.
In developing the scope of projects, basic repairs, job training facilities, campus safety,
facilities supporting Veterans, and the expansion of opportunities for local students, including the
mountain communities, to maintain access to a local affordable higher education, were prioritized.
If these facility needs are not addressed now, the District’s Colleges would be unable to remain
competitive in preparing students for high-demand jobs and careers and university transfer.
The Board of Trustees determines that San Bernardino Valley College and Crafton Hills
College MUST:
(i) Prepare students and veterans for careers in skilled trades;
(ii) Expanding workforce training for wildfire protection, snow removal, emergency
response, teachers, nurses, and other local jobs in mountain communities;
(iii) Prepare students for high-demand jobs and careers that cannot be taken away by AI;
(iv) Repair deteriorating gas lines;
(v) Maintain local affordable higher education;
(vi) Adhere to stringent FISCAL ACCOUNTABILITY safeguards including:
(a) Public disclosure of all spending
(b) All expenditures will be subject to annual independent financial audits,
(c) No funds will be used for administrators’ salaries and pensions,
(d) An independent citizens’ oversight committee will be appointed to ensure that all
funds are spent only as authorized.
The following types of projects are authorized to be undertaken at San Bernardino Valley
College, Crafton Hills College and at District Sites and Facilities:
PROVIDE LOCAL STUDENTS AN AFFORDABLE EDUCATION:
Basic Improvements Needed To Allow San Bernardino Valley College and Crafton Hills
College to provide
AFFORDABLE CAREER EDUCATION FACILITIES FOR FIREFIGHTERS AND
SKILLED TRADES
Goals and Purposes: Wildfires are getting more extreme statewide, and we recently experienced
both the Bridge and Line Fires which burned tens of thousands of acres. San Bernardino
Community College District is responsible for training most of the firefighters, paramedics, and
other emergency medical responders who protect our community. This measure is needed to
train local firefighters to keep us safe during future emergencies.
This measure includes strict accountability requirements, including public disclosure of all
spending, independent annual financial and performance audits, and a citizens’ oversight
committee to make sure all funds are used effectively, efficiently, and as authorized by voters.
By law, all funds will be used for our local community colleges and cannot be taken by county,
state or federal governments.
• Removing asbestos and mold.
• Repairing deteriorating gas lines.
• Upgrading emergency communications systems.
• Upgrading campus safety and security, including fire safety systems.
• Providing safe drinking water.
• Repairing and upgrading classrooms and labs.
• Repairing and upgrading air conditioning and heating systems.
• Earthquake retrofitting school buildings and classrooms.
PROVIDE LOCAL STUDENTS AND MOUNTAIN AREAS ACCESS TO AN AFFORDABLE
EDUCATION IN A SAFE
ENVIRONMENT:
Improvements Needed
to Provide
LOCAL JOB TRAINING PROGRAMS THAT ARE NEEDED TO PREPARE STUDENTS
FOR GOOD-PAYING CAREERS IN NURSING, TEACHING AND FIREFIGHTING
Goals and Purposes: This measure will allow residents in our mountain communities to save
money on college, avoid traffic and expensive gas prices and receive an affordable local college
education close to home. The measure will lead to access to affordable college education and job
training closer to home, hiring of local residents for new jobs, and a better trained workforce in
key fields such as nursing, teaching, and firefighting.
• Creating a community college center in the mountain area of the District.
• Upgrade classrooms and labs and career training facilities for nursing, teaching, and
firefighting.
• Improve Student Centers to provide job training, job placement, counseling, and support
services to students.
